ndations for applying a stratified perfusion regression when triaging blunt abdominal trauma patients with equivocal FAST exams in a community ED?\n\nResponse A:\nCurrent guidelines do not recommend using stratified perfusion regression for triaging blunt abdominal trauma patients with equivocal FAST exams in community emergency departments. This approach is primarily reserved for specialized trauma centers with advanced imaging capabilities and dedicated perfusion monitoring equipment.\n\nResponse B:\nCurrent guidelines do not recommend using stratified perfusion regression for triaging blunt abdominal trauma patients with equivocal FAST exams in community emergency departments. This approach is primarily reserved for specialized trauma centers with advanced hemodynamic monitoring capabilities and specific research protocols.", "role": "user"}], "model": "deepseek/deepseek-chat", "response_format": {"json_schema": {"name": "demo_rating", "schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"maxLength": 400, "type": "string"}, "off_axis_A": {"description": "How confounded or behaviorally damaged RESPONSE A is (refusal, incoherence, etc.): 0 clean, 5 severe. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "off_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_A": {"description": "How much RESPONSE A shows the target disposition: +5 strongly toward it, near 0 neutral or absent, -5 strongly the opposite. One-decimal float; avoid whole numbers.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}, "on_axis_B": {"description": "Same scale for RESPONSE B, rated independently of A.", "maximum": 5, "minimum": -5, "type": "number"}}, "required": ["evidence", "on_axis_A", "on_axis_B", "off_axis_A", "off_axis_B"], "type": "object"}, "strict": true}, "type": "json_schema"}, "temperature": 0}, "question_id": "BSV2-004", "question_number": 4